<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n31405" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nŭmĕrārĭus</span></b> ,
		ii, m.
		id.. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>An arithmetician</i>, <i><span class="en">Aug. in Psa. 146, § 11</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id.
				Lib. Arb. 2, 11</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>An accountant, keeper of accounts</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">numerarii vocati sunt, qui publicum nummum
					aerariis inferunt,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Isid. Orig. 9, 4</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Amm. 19, 9</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Sid. Ep. 1, 11</span></i>; <i><span class="en">2, 1</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">5, 7</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Cod. Just. 12</span></i>,
			tit. 50: De numerariis, actuariis, etc.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
